<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Igue festival</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Igue</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Igue festival is an annual royal festival in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-city">Benin City</a>, held at the end of the year to renew the spiritual power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oba-dynasty">Oba</a> and bless the kingdom. It forms part of the cycle of royal rituals centred on the king. It reflects the religious basis of kingship in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/igue-festival.jpg" alt="Igue festival" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: OTA11 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Igue_Festival_(Chiefs_and_the_%E1%BB%8Cba).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
